# Decision
The application will use browser local storage to save vocabulary entries and their learning statuses 

# Context
The application needs to preserve vocabulary and learning progress when the user refreshes the page or closes and reopens the application. The app is also intended to be a relatively small individual project, so a separate database and backend would add unnecessary complexity

# Alternatives Considered
Browser Local Storage - simple, no backend required, works well for small single-user application
JSON file - Easy to understand, but not practical for persitent browser-based user data
SQL database - Provides structured persistent storage but requires a backend/database setup

# Consequences
Using local storage makes the application simpler to develop and allows vocabulary to persist between sessions without requiring a server. However, the data is stored only in the user's browser, so it would not automatically synchronize between different devices.